From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:38:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell/native_raminit: Options for the margin check
 and the 2D timing

The retrain margin check and the 2D centring of the read and write
timing ran in every training. Put each behind an option, off by
default: HASWELL_NRI_MARGIN_CHECK, which measures and logs the margins
of every rank and warns about those below the retrain limits, and
HASWELL_NRI_2D_TIMING.

The margin check only reports, unless HASWELL_NRI_MARGIN_CHECK_RETRAIN
says that margins below the limits make the training run again: how
the margins of a board stand against the limits is to be seen first,
and the code that ran the training again on its status was a TODO.
With that option the training runs again once, without the
optimisations, as after a failed step or memory test, and there the
check only reports.

The 2D centring is left out of the training that is done again after
a failure, as the other steps that come after the basic training.

TEST=Build of the ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init, each option
on and off.

Change-Id: I449d92f51913f5b9659c51912ee65463552acaf0
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig         | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../native_raminit/retrain_margin_check.c     | 15 +++++++++++
 .../haswell/native_raminit/train_2d_margins.c | 19 ++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 60 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
index 9c2ad84e33..3cea56aa76 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
@@ -51,6 +51,32 @@ config HASWELL_NRI_COMMAND_VREF
 	  values that pass. Best with HASWELL_NRI_MEMORY_TEST, which trains
 	  again without this when the memory test fails.
 
+config HASWELL_NRI_MARGIN_CHECK
+	bool "Measure the read and write margins after training"
+	depends on USE_NATIVE_RAMINIT
+	help
+	  After the training, measure the read and write margins of every
+	  rank, in time and in voltage, and log them (the retrain margin
+	  check), with a warning for those below the retrain limits. It
+	  takes one to two seconds in a boot that trains.
+
+config HASWELL_NRI_MARGIN_CHECK_RETRAIN
+	bool "Train again when the margins are below the retrain limits"
+	depends on HASWELL_NRI_MARGIN_CHECK
+	help
+	  Margins below the retrain limits make the training run again,
+	  once, without its optimisations, where they are only logged.
+
+config HASWELL_NRI_2D_TIMING
+	bool "Centre the read and write timing in two dimensions"
+	depends on USE_NATIVE_RAMINIT
+	help
+	  After the command training, centre the write and the read timing
+	  again at several reference voltages, weighted by the height and
+	  the width of the eye, with the per-bit deskew. Not run in the
+	  training that is done again after a failure. Best with
+	  HASWELL_NRI_MEMORY_TEST and HASWELL_NRI_MARGIN_CHECK.
+
 config HASWELL_NRI_WRITE_VREF
 	bool "Centre the write Vref of the DIMMs after training"
 	depends on USE_NATIVE_RAMINIT
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/retrain_margin_check.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/retrain_margin_check.c
index 9eb22357a7..7b79078405 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/retrain_margin_check.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/retrain_margin_check.c
@@ -97,6 +97,9 @@ enum nri_status retrain_margin_check(struct sysinfo *ctrl)
 			.dq_pat     = BASIC_VA,
 		},
 	};
+	if (!CONFIG(HASWELL_NRI_MARGIN_CHECK))
+		return NRI_STATUS_SUCCESS;
+
 	const uint8_t loopcount = 17;
 	const bool stop_on_first_error = false;
 	setup_io_test_basic_va(ctrl, ctrl->chanmap, loopcount, NSOE);
@@ -180,6 +183,18 @@ enum nri_status retrain_margin_check(struct sysinfo *ctrl)
 		return NRI_STATUS_SUCCESS;
 
 	printk(BIOS_ERR, "***** Margin limit check failed! *****\n");
+
+	/*
+	 * Only a report unless asked otherwise: how the margins of a board
+	 * stand against these limits is to be seen first. And the training that
+	 * is done again after a failure runs without the optimisations: its
+	 * margins are what the training gives, with nothing left to leave out.
+	 */
+	if (!CONFIG(HASWELL_NRI_MARGIN_CHECK_RETRAIN) || ctrl->no_latency_optimisation) {
+		printk(BIOS_WARNING, "Margins below the retrain limits, training kept\n");
+		return NRI_STATUS_SUCCESS;
+	}
+
 	printk(RMC_DEBUG, "New limits:\nParam\tUPM\tPWR\n");
 	for (unsigned int test = 0; test < ARRAY_SIZE(test_list); test++) {
 		const enum margin_param param = test_list[test].param;
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_2d_margins.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_2d_margins.c
index 3f05ddbb04..979e3e0f10 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_2d_margins.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_2d_margins.c
@@ -559,8 +559,24 @@ void data_time_centering_2d(
 	change_1d_margin_multicast(ctrl, param_v, 0, 0, false, REG_FILE_USE_CURRENT);
 }
 
+/* Not in the training that is done again after a failure */
+static bool skip_2d_timing(const struct sysinfo *ctrl)
+{
+	if (!CONFIG(HASWELL_NRI_2D_TIMING))
+		return true;
+
+	if (ctrl->no_latency_optimisation) {
+		printk(BIOS_INFO, "2D timing centring left out\n");
+		return true;
+	}
+	return false;
+}
+
 enum nri_status train_read_timing_centering_2d(struct sysinfo *ctrl)
 {
+	if (skip_2d_timing(ctrl))
+		return NRI_STATUS_SUCCESS;
+
 	const uint8_t loopcount = 15;
 
 	bool en_per_bit;
@@ -605,6 +621,9 @@ enum nri_status train_read_timing_centering_2d(struct sysinfo *ctrl)
 
 enum nri_status train_write_timing_centering_2d(struct sysinfo *ctrl)
 {
+	if (skip_2d_timing(ctrl))
+		return NRI_STATUS_SUCCESS;
+
 	const uint8_t loopcount = 15;
 
 	bool en_per_bit;
-- 
